sp.p:
—If I wer'n't this moment call'd away, I'd—but I know your master well;
                            and if he don't punish you for this audacious libel on the idol of my
                            affections—on the lovely—the divine Honoria!

No—but I dare run from it—and I'm sure you ought to thank me, Sir Edward:
                            for now you may enjoy your evening's fête—but if I hadn't reliev'd you
                            from this little burthen,

Stand by, sir; this is some contrivance of Honoria's, but it shan't amuse
                            me from my purpose; no, I'll instantly pursue her: and for you, sir;
                            dare not to follow me; dare not to affront a privileg'd man.
